WEBVTT

00:01.465 --> 00:03.795
shinjitai
I want to believe

00:03.895 --> 00:06.955
ano hi mitsuketa hikari
In the light that I found that day

00:07.435 --> 00:10.175
kimi to kawashita
Because I still have

00:10.175 --> 00:14.835
tatta hitotsuno yakusoku ga arukara
That one promise that I made to you

00:15.245 --> 00:22.245
mou tachidomarazuni aruite yukitai
I want to keep walking, never stopping

00:23.955 --> 00:26.825
Dragon Drive

00:26.825 --> 00:32.355
uresugita kajitsu wo kajiru youni
Like biting into an overripe fruit

00:32.465 --> 00:35.435
yowai jibun ni
I was spoiling myself

00:35.435 --> 00:38.695
amaetsuzukete ita
I was giving in to my weakness

00:39.165 --> 00:43.535
kimi ni deawanakereba
If I hadn't met you

00:43.535 --> 00:45.505
ima mo
I'd still...

00:45.505 --> 00:51.845
kabe wo kowasu koto nado dekinakatta yo
...be unable to break the walls around me

00:53.545 --> 00:55.915
wasurenai
I'll never forget

00:55.915 --> 00:59.145
ano hi kanjita itami
The pain that I felt that day

00:59.455 --> 01:04.465
nido to ano basho modoritakunai
I never want to go back to that place

01:04.465 --> 01:06.055
motto tsuyoku
This strong feeling

01:06.165 --> 01:08.565
shinjitai
I want to believe

01:08.565 --> 01:11.725
ano hi mitsuketa hikari
In the light I found that day

01:12.105 --> 01:17.175
kakkowarui to warawaretemo ii
Let them laugh and call me a loser

01:17.175 --> 01:19.905
bukiyou dakara
Because I'm clumsy

01:19.905 --> 01:27.405
onaji ikikata shika erabenainda
I can only choose to live life this way

01:41.735 --> 01:43.195
Eww... What is this?!

01:43.195 --> 01:44.465
M-My body's!

01:44.835 --> 01:45.965
I can hear it!

01:45.965 --> 01:47.525
This time I can hear it clearly.

02:01.255 --> 02:02.515
Ow, ow, ow...

02:03.085 --> 02:04.655
What in the world?!

02:04.655 --> 02:06.585
What's going on here?

02:11.365 --> 02:14.485
Successor

02:14.765 --> 02:16.595
What is this place?

02:16.865 --> 02:20.735
I don't know what's going on,
but it sure feels weird here.

02:21.205 --> 02:24.905
It's as if all of the cells in my body
are sending danger signals.

02:28.415 --> 02:30.505
D-Don't worry, Chibi.

02:30.745 --> 02:34.515
I'll bet it's just a bug in the game program.

02:34.515 --> 02:35.775
It'll be fixed soon.

02:36.785 --> 02:37.945
Miss L!

02:38.355 --> 02:40.045
Miss L!

02:44.425 --> 02:46.295
That's weird.

02:46.295 --> 02:48.855
Isn't she monitoring us?

02:49.295 --> 02:51.435
Hey! Maiko!

02:51.435 --> 02:53.125
Daisuke!

02:55.575 --> 02:58.005
What's going on here?

03:02.075 --> 03:04.205
A-A skull!

03:05.315 --> 03:06.215
What's wrong, Chibi?

03:09.415 --> 03:11.855
It's Gohlaoh... covered in wounds!

03:12.485 --> 03:14.545
And Maiko's not riding him!

03:18.165 --> 03:19.145
That's...

03:19.525 --> 03:20.585
Maiko?!

03:20.695 --> 03:23.225
How did that dragon get a hold of her?!

03:24.265 --> 03:25.755
Chibi, we're going to go and rescue her!

03:43.515 --> 03:44.575
Gohlaoh...

03:45.055 --> 03:46.355
Full speed, Chibi!

03:48.425 --> 03:50.015
Hold it, you dragon!

03:50.455 --> 03:52.155
Let go of Maiko!

03:56.235 --> 03:56.995
Ow!

03:57.295 --> 03:58.565
Wait a second.

03:58.565 --> 04:00.125
Isn't this supposed to be virtual?

04:00.405 --> 04:02.895
But the pain just seems too real!

04:03.205 --> 04:04.265
This can't be.

04:08.275 --> 04:10.265
No, Chibi! Don't do that!

04:10.515 --> 04:12.445
You'll blow Maiko away as well!

04:15.255 --> 04:18.775
Chibi, let's cut him off at the pass,
and try to put a stop to him!

04:28.895 --> 04:30.835
We'll take care of you...

04:30.965 --> 04:32.225
...like this!

04:38.245 --> 04:39.605
Maiko!

04:40.845 --> 04:42.245
Leave it to me, Reiji!

04:43.075 --> 04:43.905
Daisuke!

04:45.085 --> 04:47.075
My sweet honey!

04:50.055 --> 04:51.155
All right!

04:51.155 --> 04:53.415
Now I can fight with no holds barred!

04:53.885 --> 04:55.795
Here's one that I've been holding back!

04:55.795 --> 04:57.885
This one's gonna hurt a lot!

05:06.565 --> 05:08.365
This pain I feel in my fist.

05:09.035 --> 05:10.975
Could it be that...

05:15.315 --> 05:17.035
Are you okay, Maiko?

05:17.275 --> 05:19.575
Reiji. Daisuke.

05:19.885 --> 05:21.245
That's right.

05:21.455 --> 05:24.785
I was suddenly attacked
by some strange dragon.

05:25.585 --> 05:28.385
But more importantly, where are we?

05:28.795 --> 05:30.085
Yeah, Reiji.

05:30.295 --> 05:31.985
What's going on here?

05:32.125 --> 05:35.495
I have no idea what's going on, either.

05:36.095 --> 05:36.835
Just that...

05:36.835 --> 05:38.525
Just what?

05:39.065 --> 05:40.055
Reiji?

05:42.005 --> 05:43.195
Something's coming!

05:48.775 --> 05:50.745
Wh-What are we going to do?!

05:50.945 --> 05:52.705
H-Hang on, Daisuke.

05:53.185 --> 05:55.205
Th-There's a person on it!

05:58.025 --> 06:00.755
Wh-Who are they?! Who is this person?

06:03.055 --> 06:05.025
We've come to greet you.

06:05.425 --> 06:08.485
But it seems that we didn't need
an entourage this large.

06:10.695 --> 06:11.665
Y-You're...

06:23.975 --> 06:27.415
I am the one who drew you into this world.

06:29.585 --> 06:31.555
What is this place?

06:31.955 --> 06:33.155
Rikyu.

06:33.155 --> 06:36.725
There is a parallel world that exists
in a dimension separate from Earth.

06:36.725 --> 06:38.315
That is this world.

06:38.495 --> 06:40.055
And who are you?

06:40.365 --> 06:41.625
I am Meguru.

06:42.035 --> 06:46.595
You all have been tricked
by this game called "Dragon Drive".

06:49.075 --> 06:50.625
Tricked?

06:51.845 --> 06:54.545
So, how many times do I have to tell you?!

06:54.545 --> 06:57.215
They vanished, right before our eyes!

06:57.215 --> 06:58.205
Like that!

06:58.585 --> 07:00.375
The ones who vanished were Reiji Ozora...

07:00.585 --> 07:02.915
...Maiko Yukino and Daisuke Hagiwara.

07:03.385 --> 07:06.545
I saw it with my own two eyes as well,
so there's no mistake.

07:06.785 --> 07:08.515
Could you look into it?

07:08.855 --> 07:10.855
It could be a bug in the program, right?

07:10.855 --> 07:11.845
No!

07:12.095 --> 07:14.525
There's no way that could have been a bug!

07:14.865 --> 07:18.265
As it stands, the three of them
can't be found anywhere!

07:18.605 --> 07:20.155
Something definitely happened!

07:20.365 --> 07:22.135
Something terrible!

07:22.535 --> 07:23.595
Now, calm down.

07:24.005 --> 07:27.165
This could have been
some kind of hallucination on your part.

07:27.775 --> 07:28.915
Hallucination?

07:28.915 --> 07:29.945
That's right.

07:29.945 --> 07:33.905
Dragon Drive is a game that works with,
and affects the consciousness of the player.

07:34.445 --> 07:36.215
So this sometimes happens to some people.

07:36.715 --> 07:39.815
It would be best if you two
stayed away from here for a while.

07:40.055 --> 07:42.645
Are you saying that we both
had the exact same hallucination?!

07:43.155 --> 07:48.115
Could it be that there's some sort of secret
to that training room?

07:48.235 --> 07:49.495
What are you talking about?

07:49.895 --> 07:52.665
There's no special training room here.

07:52.665 --> 07:54.635
No way!

07:54.635 --> 07:56.835
- We saw it ourselves!
- In any case...

07:56.835 --> 07:59.465
...I'll remove both of your names
from the membership list.

07:59.845 --> 08:01.475
So, go and take a break from this for a bit.

08:01.475 --> 08:02.515
What?!

08:02.515 --> 08:04.065
Is that how it's going to be?

08:06.745 --> 08:09.475
I really wonder what's going on here.

08:09.815 --> 08:12.655
It's as though they disappeared
into another dimension.

08:13.025 --> 08:14.485
Another dimension?

08:14.485 --> 08:17.015
Could it be that he was telling the truth?

08:17.455 --> 08:19.255
About what? What is it?

08:19.695 --> 08:23.465
Hey, do you know something that I don't?

08:38.315 --> 08:39.975
Wh-What's with these people?!

08:40.215 --> 08:42.245
Why are they staring at us like that?

08:42.415 --> 08:44.905
They're the ones who look weird!

08:45.125 --> 08:46.485
Hey, what do you think?

08:46.685 --> 08:49.425
What that Meguru girl just said...

08:49.425 --> 08:51.825
...about this being some sort of parallel Earth.

08:52.725 --> 08:54.665
That's ridiculous!

08:54.865 --> 08:58.795
This has got to be some new program
for a role playing game.

08:59.105 --> 09:00.435
Hey, where's Reiji?

09:02.435 --> 09:03.635
Delicious!

09:03.635 --> 09:06.105
I've never had such tasty fruit in my life!

09:06.105 --> 09:08.335
Well, ours is as fresh as it gets.

09:08.945 --> 09:11.645
By the way, you sure are dressed funny.

09:12.115 --> 09:13.485
Where are you from?

09:13.485 --> 09:15.385
Reiji, what are you doing here?!

09:15.385 --> 09:16.185
Hey!

09:16.185 --> 09:17.655
You should have some of this, Maiko!

09:17.655 --> 09:19.055
It's really good!

09:20.325 --> 09:24.555
I can't believe how you can just
go with the flow like that.

09:24.725 --> 09:26.265
That's not it.

09:26.265 --> 09:28.695
I've been thinking ever since that last fight...

09:29.165 --> 09:32.135
...that this might be a real world that we're in.

09:32.605 --> 09:37.405
Otherwise, I don't think
the taste of food would be so vivid.

09:37.905 --> 09:41.375
Enough with your weird talk.
How about you try some of this, lady?

09:41.375 --> 09:45.815
I can say that there hasn't been
a character like this in any virtual world.

09:46.285 --> 09:47.515
Please, everyone.

09:47.515 --> 09:49.045
We must keep moving.

09:49.285 --> 09:52.815
There is someone who is waiting to meet you.

09:52.925 --> 09:54.055
Waiting for us?

09:54.055 --> 09:56.855
Huh? What? What's going on?

10:12.005 --> 10:13.475
Elder!

10:13.475 --> 10:15.135
I have brought the guests.

10:15.375 --> 10:16.365
Well.

10:16.675 --> 10:19.775
So, you are the warrior
chosen by Senkohcoola?

10:20.115 --> 10:24.145
That's quite a burdensome fate to bear,
considering that you're still only a child.

10:24.785 --> 10:26.375
That's Ensui, the priestess.

10:27.085 --> 10:29.075
You can ask her all about this world.

10:29.655 --> 10:30.785
Uh, right...

10:31.125 --> 10:32.525
Um, old lady...

10:32.965 --> 10:34.625
...just what the heck is this place?

10:34.825 --> 10:37.385
It's the other Earth, Rikyu.

10:37.665 --> 10:39.465
Another Earth?

10:39.605 --> 10:42.195
Don't be ridiculous!
How can we believe that?!

10:42.475 --> 10:46.935
Originally, we intended to bring
only Senkohcoola to us.

10:47.905 --> 10:52.605
But Meguru still hasn't mastered
the Dimension Joker yet.

10:53.485 --> 10:56.815
That's why you were also
brought to this world.

10:57.115 --> 10:59.105
So, this isn't virtual after all?

10:59.355 --> 11:00.855
It's a real world?

11:00.855 --> 11:02.055
No way.

11:02.055 --> 11:03.155
But why?

11:03.155 --> 11:04.595
Why would you do that?

11:04.895 --> 11:08.895
The only thing that can save Rikyu,
the whole world itself...

11:08.895 --> 11:11.225
...is the power of Senkohcoola.

11:11.735 --> 11:15.165
It is all in order to protect
the Dragonite from RI-ON.

11:15.435 --> 11:16.975
W-Wait a minute!

11:16.975 --> 11:19.735
This "Senkohcoola" and "Dragonite"...

11:19.875 --> 11:22.205
What are you talking about?!

11:22.615 --> 11:26.845
Senkohcoola is the name of the dragon
that you control.

11:27.515 --> 11:31.955
And Senkohcoola himself
is the guardian god of Rikyu.

11:31.985 --> 11:33.155
Guardian god?

11:33.155 --> 11:34.585
You mean Chibi?!

11:36.755 --> 11:38.125
Long ago...

11:38.695 --> 11:41.785
...our world Rikyu
faced a terrible and dangerous threat.

11:42.395 --> 11:44.425
A most powerful dark dragon...

11:44.835 --> 11:47.025
...the Shinryu descended upon the land.

11:47.735 --> 11:51.405
The Shinryu's immense power
dominated all other dragons...

11:51.405 --> 11:54.235
...carrying out an orgy
of death and destruction.

11:54.745 --> 11:59.475
It was then that the Dragon of Light,
Senkohcoola, appeared.

12:00.185 --> 12:05.715
After a long battle, Senkohcoola was able
to trap Shinryu in the Dragonite.

12:07.025 --> 12:10.555
However, RI-ON hopes
to acquire that Dragonite...

12:10.555 --> 12:12.925
...and aims to resurrect Shinryu.

12:13.725 --> 12:17.395
RI-ON seeks to use Shinryu's power
to achieve their goal...

12:17.395 --> 12:20.525
...of dominating the two worlds,
both the Earth and Rikyu.

12:20.665 --> 12:22.395
Who's RI-ON?

12:22.735 --> 12:25.645
The organization that created
the Dragon Drive game.

12:25.645 --> 12:27.195
No way! It can't be!

12:27.705 --> 12:28.695
It's true.

12:29.215 --> 12:30.345
RI-ON's objective...

12:30.345 --> 12:33.975
...has been to find the best dragon masters
among the children they gather.

12:34.415 --> 12:38.015
They send these children into this world
in order to find the Dragonite.

12:38.925 --> 12:43.355
Dragon Drive is not
just an innocent game for kids to enjoy.

12:44.025 --> 12:47.795
It's a game designed to train warriors
to fight for RI-ON.

12:48.865 --> 12:52.025
But Miss L was so kind and supportive to us.

12:52.535 --> 12:55.125
How could she have been lying to us?

12:56.375 --> 12:58.005
I can't believe it.

12:58.005 --> 12:58.975
Hey, look.

12:59.345 --> 13:02.275
The moment we shut our mouths,
you start telling us this tall tale!

13:02.475 --> 13:04.275
How do you expect us to believe you?!

13:04.275 --> 13:07.645
How about you just send us
back to our world, huh?!

13:07.845 --> 13:10.515
Are you saying you don't care
what happens to this world?!

13:11.015 --> 13:13.015
I'm saying that I don't believe you!

13:13.155 --> 13:14.155
Well, I...

13:14.155 --> 13:16.685
...I really can't tell what's true and what's not.

13:18.725 --> 13:20.095
It's unfortunate...

13:20.095 --> 13:23.265
...but none of you will be able to return
to your world for some time.

13:23.265 --> 13:24.135
What?!

13:24.135 --> 13:25.395
Wh-What do you mean?!

13:25.505 --> 13:26.895
Th-That's because...

13:28.535 --> 13:29.635
So you're the ones!

13:29.635 --> 13:30.625
Huh?!

13:35.175 --> 13:36.935
Wh-What do you want?

13:37.175 --> 13:40.905
You're saying this goofy-looking guy
is the master of Senkohcoola?

13:41.915 --> 13:43.785
Huh? Is this...

13:43.785 --> 13:45.445
Is this Senkohcoola?

13:46.255 --> 13:47.245
He's tiny.

13:47.385 --> 13:48.555
Hey!

13:48.555 --> 13:50.325
Who the heck are you?!

13:50.325 --> 13:51.795
At least introduce yourself!

13:51.795 --> 13:52.915
I'm Gokaku.

13:53.625 --> 13:56.655
I'm the true successor
and master of Senkohcoola.

13:57.835 --> 13:59.765
"True successor"?

13:59.765 --> 14:00.635
What's that?

14:00.835 --> 14:02.665
Look, you listen up!

14:03.005 --> 14:07.875
Senkohcoola is the most powerful dragon
and the guardian god of our clan.

14:08.775 --> 14:13.185
And I, Gokaku, am the warrior
who will carry on as master of this dragon.

14:13.715 --> 14:15.545
Now, come! Senkohcoola!

14:22.095 --> 14:23.885
I don't think he wants to.

14:24.255 --> 14:25.995
I'll show you soon enough!

14:25.995 --> 14:30.155
I'll show you who is best suited
to be successor and master of Senkohcoola!

14:33.405 --> 14:34.505
Let's go, Komaki.

14:34.505 --> 14:35.405
R-Right!

14:35.435 --> 14:37.775
Of all the! What was that?!

14:37.775 --> 14:38.875
I'm sorry.

14:38.875 --> 14:40.635
He is a nice boy at heart.

14:41.475 --> 14:42.215
Oops.

14:42.215 --> 14:44.245
Wow, am I ever hungry.

14:44.245 --> 14:46.505
Boy, you have no sense of dramatic tension.

14:46.815 --> 14:49.685
How could you be thinking of food
at a time like this?

14:50.915 --> 14:53.855
I have a medical condition.
My stomach growls when I'm nervous.

14:53.855 --> 14:55.155
Oh, right.

14:56.155 --> 14:58.255
Meguru, offer a meal to our guests.

15:01.995 --> 15:04.235
I can't believe you can eat at a time like this.

15:04.235 --> 15:06.505
I get hungry even when I'm worried.

15:06.505 --> 15:07.705
How can I help that?

15:07.705 --> 15:10.395
But you know, I still can't believe it.

15:10.605 --> 15:12.245
That this is reality.

15:12.245 --> 15:15.365
I wonder if what she said
about RI-ON is true, too.

15:15.515 --> 15:16.735
What do you think?

15:17.045 --> 15:19.245
How do you like the food of Rikyu?

15:19.415 --> 15:23.975
Well, I prefer my food to be more flavorful,
but I can still eat this stuff.

15:24.385 --> 15:26.685
How can you say that after eating so much?

15:28.895 --> 15:30.885
Where did the guardian god go?

15:31.025 --> 15:33.395
Oh, he was there just a second ago.

15:34.525 --> 15:36.015
Th-There's big trouble!

15:36.395 --> 15:37.535
What's the matter, Komaki?!

15:37.535 --> 15:42.735
I tried to do my best to stop him,
but Gokaku has taken Senkohcoola, and!

15:42.805 --> 15:44.465
- What?!
- He took Chibisuke?!

15:45.505 --> 15:47.235
He said he was going to the Den of Goshoh!

15:48.205 --> 15:49.415
The fool!

15:49.415 --> 15:51.815
He intends to take the Fang of Goshoh!

15:51.945 --> 15:52.645
Oh, no!

15:52.645 --> 15:54.845
Hey, just what is this "Den of Goshoh"?!

15:55.045 --> 15:56.315
The Den of Goshoh...

15:57.355 --> 16:00.325
...is part of a tradition
in these parts from ancient times.

16:00.985 --> 16:04.855
If one retrieves the Fang of Goshoh
from deep in the den and returns alive...

16:05.055 --> 16:07.525
...one is accepted as a full-grown warrior.

16:07.925 --> 16:10.835
Of course, this is not an easy task.

16:12.435 --> 16:18.135
Many young warriors have recklessly tried,
only to lose their lives.

16:21.145 --> 16:26.275
Although Gokaku has been raised
as the Senkohcoola successor from infancy...

16:26.585 --> 16:28.755
...he's too inexperienced to venture there.

16:28.755 --> 16:31.785
He will become the prey
of Goshoh along with Senkohcoola.

16:31.785 --> 16:33.215
Ch-Chibi...

16:33.925 --> 16:34.985
H-Hey!

16:38.665 --> 16:40.995
Mister, I'm borrowing this dragon!

16:41.935 --> 16:43.935
- Forget it! He listens only to me.
- I'll guide you to the Den of Goshoh!

16:43.935 --> 16:45.725
- Forget it! He listens only to me.
- All right! Let's go!

16:46.305 --> 16:47.595
Hey! Reiji!

16:49.235 --> 16:51.035
Hey! Where do you think you're going?!

16:54.005 --> 16:57.175
It's the first time he's been on this dragon,
but he's already mastered it!

16:57.945 --> 17:00.215
I'm sure of it. This young man is...

17:04.585 --> 17:06.615
I see something dark up ahead.

17:06.855 --> 17:08.985
That's it! That's the Den of Goshoh!

17:10.825 --> 17:12.795
Wow, I can feel the ground tremble.

17:13.095 --> 17:14.785
That's the sound of Goshoh moving around.

17:16.595 --> 17:17.585
Chibi.

17:35.655 --> 17:38.675
Why won't you transform, Senkohcoola?

17:39.525 --> 17:43.145
Thanks to you,
Goshoh got one of our dragons.

17:45.095 --> 17:47.825
I am your true master,
the rightful successor.

17:48.195 --> 17:49.755
Why don't you obey me?

17:50.535 --> 17:52.495
What's he got that I don't?

17:53.305 --> 17:57.105
I've been trained and educated
to be the successor since I was born.

17:57.775 --> 17:59.965
I am far more qualified, from birth!

18:00.605 --> 18:06.065
There's no way that some idiot
from another world could be the successor.

18:06.585 --> 18:08.745
That is a fact that cannot be changed!

18:09.115 --> 18:13.215
And you still see him as the successor?

18:14.985 --> 18:16.545
H-He's coming!

18:26.365 --> 18:27.625
Chibi!

18:43.785 --> 18:45.155
You can do it, Chibi!

18:47.585 --> 18:48.455
Y-You?!

18:48.455 --> 18:50.395
Let's go, Chibi!

19:04.735 --> 19:07.405
Th-That's Senkohcoola?

19:07.805 --> 19:10.305
Gokaku! Now's your chance to get away!

19:10.715 --> 19:11.505
R-Right.

19:15.115 --> 19:16.445
Be careful, Reiji!

19:16.655 --> 19:18.985
That's lava that Goshoh creates
within his body!

19:19.085 --> 19:20.745
Huh? Lava?

19:24.395 --> 19:25.685
Whoa, that was close!

19:25.995 --> 19:28.185
Chibi, we've got to fight back!

19:30.695 --> 19:31.925
No! You mustn't attack!

19:35.135 --> 19:35.905
What?!

19:35.905 --> 19:36.925
He's absorbing it!

19:37.135 --> 19:38.665
Get out of there, Reiji!

19:39.105 --> 19:40.335
What the?!

19:40.545 --> 19:45.065
Goshoh can absorb any attack,
and bounce it back many times stronger!

19:45.275 --> 19:47.375
No. He'll get them at this rate!

19:48.815 --> 19:50.305
All right, then!

19:53.785 --> 19:55.155
That's reckless, Reiji!

19:55.155 --> 19:56.525
Isn't he listening?!

20:02.635 --> 20:04.335
All right! This is the final blow!

20:04.335 --> 20:05.955
Go! Chibi!

20:16.315 --> 20:17.535
The Fang of Goshoh.

20:18.145 --> 20:20.805
I can't believe he destroyed Goshoh.

20:26.685 --> 20:28.175
Gokaku! Wait!

20:28.525 --> 20:29.685
It's true.

20:29.925 --> 20:35.765
Right now, it's true that the guy from Earth
may be most suited to Senkohcoola.

20:36.365 --> 20:37.665
But...

20:37.665 --> 20:39.065
But one day...

20:39.065 --> 20:42.695
...I will become a successor
worthy of Senkohcoola.

20:42.875 --> 20:44.035
And I'll master Senkohcoola.

20:44.405 --> 20:45.965
The Senkohcoola.

20:49.845 --> 20:50.745
Gokaku.

20:59.525 --> 21:00.715
There's no mistake.

21:01.085 --> 21:02.715
This young man has something.

21:03.225 --> 21:05.085
A power that no other possesses.

21:06.525 --> 21:08.725
Hey, where did you go?!

21:08.865 --> 21:10.195
We were worried, you know!

21:10.465 --> 21:13.335
- You idiot!
- Uh, sorry. Sorry.

21:13.805 --> 21:18.265
That is why he was chosen
to be the master of Senkohcoola.

21:19.675 --> 21:24.905
However, by now RI-ON must realize
that Reiji and his friends have come to Rikyu.

21:25.145 --> 21:28.015
I'm sure they're moving quickly
with their plans by now.

21:29.755 --> 21:32.345
Come in, Hikaru Himuro.

21:55.975 --> 21:58.715
taikutsu datta
I was bored

21:58.715 --> 22:01.485
okubyou datta
I was a coward

22:01.485 --> 22:05.445
dareka wo jibun wo kizutsukete ita
I was hurting someone and myself

22:06.885 --> 22:09.655
tsuyogari itte
I tried to hide my weakness

22:09.655 --> 22:11.855
wagamama itte
I was being selfish

22:12.295 --> 22:16.425
doushiyoumonai kimochi mamoritsuzukete
Protecting the uncontrollable feeling

22:17.835 --> 22:20.505
otona ni natte
I became an adult

22:20.505 --> 22:23.235
kimi to deatte
Then I met you

22:23.235 --> 22:27.235
mune no sumikko yawarakaku natte
My heart got softened

22:28.545 --> 22:31.045
setsunaku natta
Longing for love

22:31.045 --> 22:34.045
dakishime atta
We embraced each other

22:34.045 --> 22:38.955
hakkiri mamorubeki mono wo mitsuketa
I finally knew what I wanted to protect

22:39.585 --> 22:42.325
tatta hitotsu no yuuki ga
Only one courage

22:42.325 --> 22:45.095
tatta hitotsu no kotoba ga
Just one word

22:45.095 --> 22:49.755
futari owaranai yume e to hakobu
Take us to an endless dream

22:50.465 --> 22:53.235
hon no chiisana yasashisa ga
Only a small kindness

22:53.235 --> 22:55.905
hon no wazuka na sasayaki ga
Only a small whisper

22:55.905 --> 23:00.565
futari wo sotto tsutsunde kureru
Wrap us gently

23:01.205 --> 23:05.735
zutto konomama asa ga kurumade
Until the morning comes

23:06.645 --> 23:12.345
zutto konomama asa ga kurumade
Until the morning comes

23:14.785 --> 23:17.345
Next Episode

23:18.125 --> 23:19.885
I guess this is what they call "Destiny".

23:20.565 --> 23:24.555
It means that I'm going to be the savior,
a glorious hero!

23:25.295 --> 23:28.135
What? You say there's someone
already wanting to challenge us?

23:28.705 --> 23:30.635
Guess he doesn't know what he's up against.

23:31.305 --> 23:32.035
What?!

23:32.035 --> 23:33.475
Who is that guy?!

23:33.475 --> 23:35.535
He looks wild and violent and dangerous!

23:36.045 --> 23:39.035
Next time on Dragon Drive,
"Dragonic Heaven".

23:39.345 --> 23:41.685
Um, do you think we can just talk it over?

23:41.685 --> 23:41.815
Dragonic Heaven

23:41.815 --> 23:44.415
Dragonic Heaven
I guess not.
